      "writtenOn": "2021-06-24T13:51:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "is there a criteria we can read from the BT device to distinguish between DEVICE_OUT_BLE_HEADSET and DEVICE_OUT_BLE_SPEAKER",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 457,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 457,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "08c06e6da29c0b225003546befcb2d9e698fd96d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ee30d8a0_856ae175",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/audio/AudioDeviceInventory.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 457,
      "author": {
        "id": 1687135
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-28T11:38:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is quite tricky in LE Audio since here we represent group of devices as device.\n\nI guess we could rely on devices Appearance but I\u0027m not sure if it\u0027s best way how to solve it.\n\nThere can be done matching in service e.g.:\n1) 1 or 2 earbuds (each appearance from category Wearable Audio Device) \u003d HEADSET\n2) 1 or 2 speakers (each appearance from category Audio Sink) \u003d SPEAKER\n\nBut what to do if those appearances would be mixed or missing in any of group devices ?\n\nI\u0027ve assumed here HEADSET since there is no further logic distinguishing HEADSET from SPEAKER.",
      "parentUuid": "674ecff4_298efe4e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 457,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 457,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "08c06e6da29c0b225003546befcb2d9e698fd96d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
